{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4716",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufb10 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which participate in the same metabolic process, leading to the participation of Ndufb10 in this activity. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Metformin may influence Ndufb10, possibly through modulation of the ubiquinone-dependent respiratory chain. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, with Metformin's interaction with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 serving as a critical bridge to Ndufb10. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a direct interaction between Metformin and Ndufb10, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence underscores a plausible, mechanistically sound pathway that links Metformin to Ndufb10, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance of this relationship.",
